35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found that chasing small payments takes a huge amount of time for the treasurer. It's much easier to collect once a year.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Most of our costs are fixed, like hall hire and insurance. We pay those regardless of attendance.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"I've learned that tiered grades caused friction in the past, and some potential members are scared off by a large upfront annual fee.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,It seems charging per event kills the habit of coming to weekday meetings. People stop feeling like they belong.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My suspicions were right. A tiny fraction of us do everything, while others pay and never show up. It's completely uneven.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, if a big annual fee is scary, but small fees are a nightmare for the treasurer, what do we do?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"We also have people struggling to pay the annual fee all at once, according to the bank statements.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,We need a balance. We can't have a system that creates social tiers or discourages new blood.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. If we charge per activity, the regulars feel it's a chore and the casuals feel guilty.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"The ""regulars"" are the ones doing the setup and locking up. They are subsidizing the ghosts.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,I really don't want the next treasurer to quit because of the workload. Hand-calculating mid-year joins is also a pain.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Since 70% of costs are fixed, a purely activity-based system is financially risky. We can't guess the income.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"Tiered membership sounds like it would just repeat the old mistakes of making people feel ""lesser.""","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,I agree with Minako. Let's keep it simple so people just show up without overthinking the cost.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Simple is fine, but fair is better. Why should the ghosts get the same deal as the workers?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
